From 60a4d92c069ccf02b44db896d3609d3ab443fed0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mildstorm <mildstorm@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:58:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add the ALS CP/M Card (Advanced Logic Systems "The CP/M
 Card")

A 6 MHz Z80B with 64K of its own, the card CP/M Plus 3.01 was sold with,
modelled from its schematic and board photos
(https://github.com/mildstorm/TheCPMCard, which also has the disks).

- ALSCPMCard: $Cnxx write toggles the bus (as the SoftCard), bank latch on
  any Z80 OUT, U26 page map (Z80 + $9000, $Cxxx/$Fxxx swapped) in bank 0,
  card RAM in bank 1 and at $F000-$FFFF, IN returns D0 = /IRQ, 62 Hz tick
  on /INT acknowledged with $F7 (RST 30h), snapshot with RAM and registers
- Z80VICE: a Z80Board hook for memory, I/O, clock and a level /INT
  (IM 0/1/2, EI delay, HALT); without one the SoftCard runs as before.
  6 MHz in bank 1 with the M1 stretch, 3 MHz in bank 0.
- Slot option "ALS CP/M Card"; command line -sN cpmcard, and -sN z80 or
  softcard for the SoftCard. Only one Z80 card at a time.

Tested: CP/M Plus 3.01C boots, DIR and DATE (running clock) work;
Microsoft CP/M 2.20B on the SoftCard unchanged.
